From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NorkzYT <richard@pcscorp.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:21:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approvals): honour permanent command_allowlist pattern
 keys in -q, cron and unattended runs

An operator's "Always" answer stores the dangerous-pattern key in
command_allowlist. Interactive sessions honoured it; _unattended_deny() never
consulted it, so a Kanban worker (`hermes chat -q`) kept denying commands the
operator had approved for good (e.g. `python3 -c`). Permanent entries now apply
there too; session-only approvals, the hardline floor and the tirith scan are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../tools/test_single_query_approval_mode.py  | 66 ++++++++++++++++++-
 tools/approval.py                             | 15 +++++
 2 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

